0.06 0.17 0.36 rg 0.06 0.17 0.36 RG 0.00 803.89 595.28 38.00 re f
BT 1 1 1 rg /F2 9 Tf 48.00 817.89 Td (HealthGuard AI - Senior Software Engineer / GenAI Interview Guide) Tj ET
BT 0.25 0.29 0.36 rg /F1 8 Tf 48.00 28.00 Td (Healthcare GenAI | RAG | Voice Assistant | Patient Safety Chatbot) Tj ET
BT 0.25 0.29 0.36 rg /F1 8 Tf 502.28 28.00 Td (Page 7) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 777.89 Td (The system includes a responsive dashboard, chatbot, voice assistant, document upload, RAG indexing, and) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 765.39 Td (report generation. The backend validates auth and consent, stores chat memory by user and conversation,) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 752.89 Td (runs NLP and safety checks, retrieves RAG context, and uses an LLM abstraction only when useful.) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.39 0.40 rg /F2 11.5 Tf 48.00 735.39 Td (5-minute architecture explanation) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 718.39 Td (Start with browser flows: auth, dashboard, assessment, chat, voice, upload, and reports. FastAPI routes) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 705.89 Td (enforce user and role checks. Services handle chat/NLP/safety/RAG/LLM/report/PDF/storage. Uploaded) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 693.39 Td (documents become user-scoped chunks. Reports use triage, risk scoring, RAG context, optional Gemini) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 680.89 Td (enhancement, fail-closed behavior, audit logs, and PDF generation.) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.39 0.40 rg /F2 11.5 Tf 48.00 663.39 Td (Senior Engineer / GenAI role) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 646.39 Td (As a Senior Engineer, emphasize modular architecture, testing, memory isolation, RBAC, performance, and) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 633.89 Td (production hardening. As a GenAI Developer, emphasize RAG, prompts, NLP extraction, safety guardrails,) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48.00 621.39 Td (model abstraction, and evaluation.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 16 Tf 48.00 599.89 Td (31. Cross Questions and Answers) Tj ET
0.82 0.85 0.88 RG 0.6 w 48.00 591.89 m 547.28 591.89 l S
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 577.89 Td (1. Why RAG?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 564.89 Td (RAG grounds answers in uploaded documents and approved knowledge without training private patient data into) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 552.89 Td (the model.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 535.89 Td (2. Why not only LLM?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 522.89 Td (LLMs can hallucinate. HealthGuard uses deterministic safety rules, NLP intent extraction, RAG context, and) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 510.89 Td (tests.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 493.89 Td (3. How do you avoid hallucination?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 480.89 Td (Use scoped retrieval, citations, safe base answers, refusal rules, and prompt regression tests.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 463.89 Td (4. How do embeddings work?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 450.89 Td (Chunks become numeric vectors. Similar vectors represent semantically related content.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 433.89 Td (5. What vector DB did you use?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 420.89 Td (The demo supports local embedding JSON and is ready for pgvector or Qdrant.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 403.89 Td (6. How does chunking work?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 390.89 Td (Documents are split into overlapping chunks with metadata for precise retrieval.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 373.89 Td (7. How do you handle latest records?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 360.89 Td (Fetch latest chat rows DESC, limit them, then reverse to chronological order.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 343.89 Td (8. How do you isolate user data?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 330.89 Td (Every chat, report, and RAG query filters by user_id and conversation_id or ownership.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 313.89 Td (9. How do you handle voice input?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 300.89 Td (Continuous speech recognition captures interim text and sends the final transcript to lightweight chat mode.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 283.89 Td (10. Why async?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 270.89 Td (Async improves throughput for I/O waits such as LLM, DB, SMTP, and vector search.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 253.89 Td (11. Async vs threading vs multiprocessing?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 240.89 Td (Async handles waiting I/O, threads handle blocking I/O, and multiprocessing handles CPU-heavy parsing/OCR.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 223.89 Td (12. How do decorators work?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 210.89 Td (Decorators wrap functions to add behavior such as auth checks, logging, caching, or rate limits.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 193.89 Td (13. How do you handle 5000 Excel uploads?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 180.89 Td (Save files, create jobs, process with Redis/Celery workers, use read_only mode, batch inserts, and progress) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 168.89 Td (tracking.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 151.89 Td (14. What metrics do you monitor?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 138.89 Td (Latency, P95, errors, token usage, cost, LLM latency, vector latency, RAG hit rate, queue length, and) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 126.89 Td (feedback.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 109.89 Td (15. How do you test RAG?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 96.89 Td (Use known documents, expected chunks, citation checks, isolation tests, and prompt regressions.) Tj ET
endstream
