0.06 0.17 0.36 rg 0.06 0.17 0.36 RG 0.00 803.89 595.28 38.00 re f
BT 1 1 1 rg /F2 9 Tf 48.00 817.89 Td (HealthGuard AI - Senior Software Engineer / GenAI Interview Guide) Tj ET
BT 0.25 0.29 0.36 rg /F1 8 Tf 48.00 28.00 Td (Healthcare GenAI | RAG | Voice Assistant | Patient Safety Chatbot) Tj ET
BT 0.25 0.29 0.36 rg /F1 8 Tf 502.28 28.00 Td (Page 11) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 777.89 Td (84. How do you handle streaming responses?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 764.89 Td (Streaming sends token-like chunks so users see progress before the final answer is complete.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 747.89 Td (85. How do you handle rate limiting?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 734.89 Td (Rate limits protect APIs from abuse and accidental repeated requests.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 717.89 Td (86. How do you handle upload scanning?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 704.89 Td (Uploads are checked for size, type, suspicious content, and extraction viability before indexing.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 687.89 Td (87. How do you handle unsupported browser voice?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 674.89 Td (The UI shows a clear message and allows manual transcript typing.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 657.89 Td (88. How do you handle ASR failure?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 644.89 Td (The backend returns a safe generic transcription error without leaking provider internals.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 627.89 Td (89. How do you handle local vector store?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 614.89 Td (The demo can store embeddings as JSON locally for simple semantic retrieval.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 597.89 Td (90. How do you handle pgvector?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 584.89 Td (pgvector is useful when PostgreSQL is already the primary database and vector search should stay nearby.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 567.89 Td (91. How do you handle Qdrant?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 554.89 Td (Qdrant is suitable for a dedicated scalable vector service with payload filtering and fast retrieval.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 537.89 Td (92. How do you handle prompt output tests?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 524.89 Td (Prompt regression tests assert style, refusal language, shortness, stages, and no unsafe content.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 507.89 Td (93. How do you handle RAG evaluation?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 494.89 Td (RAG evals check that known queries retrieve expected chunks and cite correct sources.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 477.89 Td (94. How do you handle backups?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 464.89 Td (Production needs database, object storage, vector index, and audit log backups with restore drills.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 447.89 Td (95. How do you handle rollback?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 434.89 Td (Rollback returns the system to a known-good deployment if smoke tests or metrics fail.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 417.89 Td (96. How do you handle model upgrades?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 404.89 Td (Model upgrades require prompt regression, safety, RAG, and cost/latency tests before release.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 387.89 Td (97. How do you handle token optimization?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 374.89 Td (Keep prompts short, retrieve only relevant chunks, limit memory, and choose compact output.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 357.89 Td (98. How do you handle small classifier model?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 344.89 Td (A smaller model or rules can classify intent cheaply before calling a larger model.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 327.89 Td (99. How do you handle large final model?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 314.89 Td (A larger model is reserved for final synthesis when context and safety checks justify it.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 9.4 Tf 48.00 297.89 Td (100. How do you handle hallucination rate?) Tj ET
BT 0.07 0.09 0.13 rg /F1 9.0 Tf 48.00 284.89 Td (Track unsupported claims and improve prompts/retrieval when the rate rises.) Tj ET
BT 0.06 0.17 0.36 rg /F2 16 Tf 48.00 263.89 Td (32. Final Summary) Tj ET
